<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Imre Szapolyai</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1487">1487</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Emeric Szapolyai, Emeric Zápolya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Imre Szapolyai was a Hungarian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a> and a leading commander under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthias-corvinus">Matthias Corvinus</a>. He served as ban of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jajce">Jajce</a> and of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavonia">Slavonia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a>, defending the southern frontier against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, and later as palatine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. He founded the fortune of the Szapolyai family, whose nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-zapolya">John Zápolya</a> became king.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/imre-szapolyai.jpg" alt="Imre Szapolyai" width="320" height="612" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:Szegedi_László · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emeric_Z%C3%A1polya_gravestone.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
